# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DawnScribe — files kept in the repo but NOT deployed to dawnscribe.com
#
# Anything in the project root is served as a static file by Vercel, so an
# internal note sitting next to index.html is a public URL. These entries
# stay in version control (still on disk, still in git) and simply never
# reach the CDN.
#
# Do NOT add: middleware.js, vercel.json, robots.txt, site.webmanifest,
# og-default.png, or api/. Those have no inbound links from the HTML but are
# loaded by the platform, by crawlers, or by absolute URL, so ignoring them
# would break edge rendering, the sitemap rewrite, or social previews.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Internal documentation. EMAIL-SYSTEM.md was reachable at
# /EMAIL-SYSTEM.md and names cron jobs, edge functions, tables and the
# Resend quota constraint — no credentials, but no reason to publish it.
*.md

# Design/spec reference pages. Not linked from anywhere in the site; these
# are working documents for building the real artwork.
dawnscribe-pendant-reference.html

# Local scratch that should never ship if it ever lands in the root.
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
